A Subquery is a query within another SQL query and embedded within the WHERE clause.
• A subquery is enclosed in parentheses.
• A subquery is a query within another query. The outer query is known as the main query, and the inner query is known as a subquery.
• In the Subquery, ORDER BY command cannot be used. But GROUP BY command can be used to perform the same function as ORDER BY command.
 
• A subquery can be placed in a number of SQL clauses like WHERE clause, FROM clause, HAVING clause.
• You can use Subquery with SELECT, UPDATE, INSERT, DELETE statements along with the operators like =, <, >, >=, <=, IN, BETWEEN, etc

If the inner query DOES NOT use outer query columns Non-Correlated Subquery

If the inner query USES outer query columns Correlated Subquery 

There are two types of subqueries 
------------------------------------
1.Non correlated sub queries.(normal subqueries)Nested query
 
2.Correlated sub queries.
 
1.Non correlated sub questions (normal subqueries)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
●In Non correlated sub queries Inner query runs first, and only once. Outer query is executed with result from Inner query 
●It is a Bottom up approach.
●In this mostly in ,not in , equal this are used
    

SELECT name
FROM products
WHERE id IN (
    SELECT product_id
    FROM order_details
    GROUP BY product_id
    HAVING SUM(quantity) > 2
);


SELECT name
FROM users
WHERE id IN (
    SELECT user_id
    FROM orders
    WHERE total_amount > (
        SELECT AVG(total_amount)
        FROM orders
    )
);



SELECT name
FROM products
WHERE id IN (
    SELECT id
    FROM products
    WHERE stock = 0
);

2.Correlated sub queries.
----------------------------------  
●Outer query Executes first and for every outer query row inner query is executed
● It is a Top down approach.
●In this ,exist and not exist are mostly used.

SELECT DISTINCT u.name
FROM users u
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM orders o
    WHERE o.user_id = u.id
      AND o.total_amount > (
          SELECT AVG(total_amount)
          FROM orders
          WHERE user_id = u.id
      )
);


SELECT o.id
FROM orders o
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM payments p
    WHERE p.order_id = o.id
      AND p.payment_status = 'SUCCESS'
);


| Feature     | Non-Correlated     | Correlated         |
| ----------- | ------------------ | ------------------ |
| Runs        | Once               | Multiple times     |
| Used for    | Reports, analytics | Validation, checks |
| Operators   | `IN`, `=`          | `EXISTS`           |
| Performance | Faster             | Slower             |

